            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for a lock of hair, then the Gujarati for the parting of the hair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: વાન",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "વાન — vān — \"complexion; skin colour\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દાદા કહે છે કે મારો વાન મારી માતાનો છે. dādā kahe che ke māro vān mārī mātāno che. Grandfather says that I have my mother's complexion."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "વાન (vān) is inherited from Sanskrit varṇa, \"appearance, colour\"; CDIAL lists the Gujarati word, \"colour\" (CDIAL 11338)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
